@startuml
!include ../../common/eztrade-style.puml

title EZTrade - Logical Spring Modulith Dependencies

package "Spring Modulith application" {
  component "user\n@ApplicationModule" as User EZ_BACKEND
  component "security\nallowed: user :: api" as Security EZ_BACKEND
  component "market\n@ApplicationModule" as Market EZ_BACKEND
  component "trading\nallowed: market :: api" as Trading EZ_BACKEND
  component "wallet\nallowed: trading :: events,\nuser :: api" as Wallet EZ_BACKEND
  component "portfolio\nallowed: trading :: events,\nwallet :: events,\nmarket :: api" as Portfolio EZ_BACKEND
  component "notifications\nallowed: trading :: events,\nportfolio :: events,\nwallet :: events" as Notifications EZ_BACKEND
}

Security --> User : LoadUserForSecurityPort\nUserOwnerLookup via api
Trading --> Market : MarketPriceLookupPort\ncurrentPrice(symbol)
Portfolio --> Market : MarketPriceLookupPort\nvaluation
Wallet --> User : UserOwnerLookupPort\ntransfer recipient lookup

Trading ..> Wallet : OrderPlacedEvent\nOrderCancelledEvent\nOrderExecutionRequestEvent
Wallet ..> Trading : OrderExecutedEvent\n(after settlement)
Trading ..> Portfolio : OrderExecutedEvent
Wallet ..> Portfolio : AvailableCashUpdatedEvent
Trading ..> Notifications : order events
Wallet ..> Notifications : InsufficientFundsEvent
Portfolio ..> Notifications : PortfolioValuationUpdatedEvent

note bottom
Evidence: package-info.java files declare allowedDependencies.
ModulithStructureTest verifies the module graph during the test phase.
Solid arrows represent direct port/API dependencies; dashed arrows represent Spring domain events.
end note

@enduml
